drafter-1a: host-side confidence trim of the DFlash2 verify length (stage 0).

Research experiment for docs/research/deepinfer/drafter.md drafter-1 (stage 0; spec-2 is the
device-side twin). NOT in patches/series. Written against the image's installed (already
patched) vLLM: dflash2/speculator.py there carries patches/dflash2-lookup-drafting.patch.

Off unless VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM is 1 or 2; with it unset (0) next_num_draft_tokens returns
exactly what the lookup returns today, no graphs are added, and the new env names are left out
of the torch.compile cache key, so a default boot is the stock image.

What it does, once per step on the host (DFlash2Speculator.next_num_draft_tokens):
  - only when the lookup's decision is the drafter's own block (never trims the lookup's long
    block, never a drafter-free chain step) and draft_max_seq_len >= CONF_TRIM_MIN_CTX;
  - conf_j = max softmax of the realised selector scores at walk step j (candidate_sampler.scores,
    the buffer vLLM's acceptance estimator reads), 1 at positions the lookup supplied;
  - survival s_k = prod_{j<=k} conf_j, max over the batch;
  - keep k = #{k : s_k >= thr}, rounded UP to an allowed count (CONF_TRIM_LENS, default
    MIN_K..block), with thr = VLLM_DFLASH2_VERIFY_MS_PER_TOKEN x tokens-per-ms (EMA of emitted
    tokens over host step period, read through pinned memory, no sync), or a fixed
    VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM_THR. This is check c3-c5's cost-aware threshold.
  - CONF_TRIM=1 reads s_k fresh (a .cpu() that waits for the draft pass: the host loses its
    overlap with the drafter, ~host prep time per step); CONF_TRIM=2 uses the previous step's
    s_k from pinned memory (no sync, one step stale, which spec-2's sim says is worth ~0).
cudagraph_utils.py captures a uniform decode graph for every allowed trimmed length, otherwise
those steps would fall to the mixed/piecewise path.

Needs synchronous scheduling (--no-async-scheduling, launcher ASYNC_SCHED=0): vLLM feeds the
worker's draft count back to the scheduler only there. Lossless; greedy text may still move by
rounding across verify widths (drafter/README.md:116-120). Refuse at CTX=huge with prefix
caching (KVarN varlen corruption, single-user/start_qwen.sh, the LOOKUP_ADAPTIVE comment).

Knobs: VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM (0/1/2), VLLM_DFLASH2_VERIFY_MS_PER_TOKEN, VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM_THR,
VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM_MIN_CTX (32768), VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM_MIN_K (2),
VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM_LENS (""), VLLM_DFLASH2_CONF_TRIM_LOG_SEC (30; logs the chosen-count
histogram, thr, tokens/ms and context: the evidence that the trim engaged).

